because those are the things that only they do. And there are certainly there are craftsmen and comics who know just how to make it sing and compose it with great precision and orchestrate the line so that there is no mumbling so that there is no noise. And I love them too, but the imperfections I think are part of what people are drawn to in my medium. It is an imperfect medium because it is the creation of an imperfect species. And the idiosyncrasies of cartoonists like, you know, say Robert Crom or Charles Schultz, these are the things that I dissecting the world of visual communication relate to close family members who are blind?
因为那些是只有他们才能做到的事情。当然，漫画界也有一些工匠，他们知道如何让画面歌唱，以极高的精确度进行构图，并编排线条，使得没有喃喃自语，没有杂音。我也很喜欢他们，但这些不完美我认为正是人们被我的媒介所吸引的部分原因。它是一种不完美的媒介，因为它是某个不完美的物种所创造的。而漫画家们的特质，比如，罗伯特·克鲁姆（Robert Crumb）或查尔斯·舒尔茨（Charles Schulz），这些我在解剖视觉传达世界时，与那些失明的近亲家属有何关联？

