00:25:53.000 --> 00:26:37.000
I ask that question and get a really cool answer from Scott McLeod right after this. You really take in the world with a lot of attention to the visual cues and graphic interface, and you happen to have a blind father, you have a blind daughter. How has that affected the way you perceive the world and even like how you relate to them? The condition that both my father who's been deceased for some time and my daughter have is called Stargart's disease. It's an inherited condition and it's a form of macular degeneration. Their central vision is what wasn't as affected.
