00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:48.000
trying to access that information. And she had come upon obstacles trying to access that information. And it really illuminated the fact that though they were different obstacles that the principal was the same, that bad design is committing the same moral sin as a lack of access for those with disabilities. In fact, really, at the end of the day, we all have disabilities. We all have cognitive limits. We all have limits of our senses. And a failure to recognize the multiplicity of barriers that stand between us and what sometimes is life-saving information is an urgent public work that needs to take place.
在试图获取该信息时遇到了障碍。这确实阐明了一个事实，即尽管它们是不同的障碍，但原则是相同的：糟糕的设计所犯下的道德罪过，与剥夺残疾人获取信息的权利是一样的。事实上，说到底，我们所有人其实都有残疾。我们所有人都有认知局限。我们所有人都有感官局限。而未能认识到在我们与有时能救命的信息之间存在的重重障碍的多样性，是一项亟待开展的紧迫公共工作。

